## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/neural_layertomask_sam2.html
- Summary (EN): Creates an image segmentation mask from prompts using Meta's SAM 2 neural network. Positive and negative point prompts, or an optional bounding box, define the objects to segment.
- Résumé (FR) : Produit un masque de segmentation d'image à partir de points positifs ou négatifs et d'une boîte optionnelle, grâce au réseau SAM 2 de Meta, avec un seuil binaire facultatif.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the image to segment; RGBA, UV and mono inputs are converted to RGB", "mask (optional): a per-pixel confidence mask, scaled by the Mask parameter", "embeddings (optional): a precomputed image encoding, reused to avoid recomputing the most expensive step", "points (optional): prompt points, interpreted by world-space location and a prompt string attribute"]

- Key parameters: ["Model: SAM2 Large (most accurate, slower), SAM2 Tiny (faster, less accurate) or Custom (your own encoder and decoder ONNX files)", "Download Models: fetches the pre-trained model files", "Units: Image space, Texture space or Pixels for point and box coordinates", "Points / Point Coords / Negative: prompt points; negative points mark areas to exclude", "Bounding Box / BBox Lower Left / BBox Upper Right: box prompt", "Resample Behavior: Stretch to Fit or Fit Minimally, for images that do not match the model's 1024x1024 input", "Color Transform: optional OCIO conversion before processing", "Clean Up (TVD Iterations, TVD Speed): smooths the output mask", "Upsampling Filter: filter used to scale the mask back to the original resolution", "Mask Threshold: converts the soft mask to binary; when off, raw soft values are output", "Preview Color: overlay colour for the mask preview in the viewer", "Execution Provider and Device ID: Automatic, CPU, CUDA, DirectML or CoreML, and the GPU"]

- Caveats: ["Click Download Models after a fresh Houdini installation before the node works.", "The page advises against a binary 0 or 1 mask input and recommends a soft mask.", "If a points input is wired, the node uses those points and then appends the Points parameter values. A bounding box set on the node replaces the one in the input.", "Reused embeddings only work with the same model size that created them.", "Points without a prompt attribute default to positive.", "CUDA requires separately installed CUDA and cuDNN. DirectML is Windows only, and CoreML is macOS only."]

